1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,555
Saint James Power Station:

2
00:00:02,635 --> 00:00:05,675
The Coal-Fired Station of 1926

3
00:00:05,675 --> 00:00:09,447
Ask a Singaporean about
Saint James Power Station and

4
00:00:09,527 --> 00:00:13,525
you will likely hear about
a nightclub, or about Dyson.

5
00:00:13,525 --> 00:00:17,250
Both answers are right,
and both skip the point.

6
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:20,827
The red-brick building at
HarbourFront began as a

7
00:00:20,907 --> 00:00:24,857
coal-fired power station —
Singapore's first municipal

8
00:00:24,937 --> 00:00:29,037
power station — and its first
generator was commissioned

9
00:00:29,117 --> 00:00:32,475
a century ago, on the
30th of September 1926.

10
00:00:32,475 --> 00:00:36,425
For fifty years it made
the town's electricity.

11
00:00:36,425 --> 00:00:40,148
The parties and the technology
headquarters came later,

12
00:00:40,228 --> 00:00:44,100
and they are only the building's
second and third lives.

13
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:48,250
Electricity came to
Singapore in small pieces.

14
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:52,495
In 1878 the Tanjong Pagar Dock
Company built a small power

15
00:00:52,575 --> 00:00:57,192
station outside its dock and put
up an arc lamp at the wharves,

16
00:00:57,272 --> 00:01:01,075
so that ships could be
worked and watched at night.

17
00:01:01,075 --> 00:01:05,082
A generation later, the
tramway-era station on Mackenzie

18
00:01:05,162 --> 00:01:08,805
Road was generating for
the electric trams by 1905,

19
00:01:08,885 --> 00:01:13,257
and in 1906 its current lit
Raffles Place and the Esplanade —

20
00:01:13,337 --> 00:01:17,710
the town's first electric street
lamps, with the Municipality

21
00:01:17,790 --> 00:01:21,950
buying power in bulk and laying
the distribution network.

22
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:27,150
By the early 1920s that
arrangement had run out of road.

23
00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:31,845
Mackenzie Road was overtaxed and
could not grow, and in 1921 the

24
00:01:31,925 --> 00:01:36,769
Municipal Engineer-in-Chief warned
that "the backward state of the

25
00:01:36,849 --> 00:01:41,550
electrical situation is holding
back the progress of the town".

26
00:01:41,550 --> 00:01:45,173
Singapore needed a proper
power station, built for the

27
00:01:45,253 --> 00:01:49,025
town rather than borrowed
from the docks and the trams.

28
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:53,849
In October 1923 the Municipal
Commissioners sent the London

29
00:01:53,929 --> 00:01:59,000
consulting engineers Preece,
Cardew and Rider to find a site.

30
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,558
They chose Cape Saint James,
a tidal-swamp headland

31
00:02:02,638 --> 00:02:05,625
on Telok Blangah Bay
beside Keppel Harbour,

32
00:02:05,705 --> 00:02:09,200
on land that had once
belonged to the Temenggong.

33
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:12,150
The reasons were practical ones.

34
00:02:12,150 --> 00:02:15,150
The sea provided cooling water.

35
00:02:15,150 --> 00:02:19,200
Wharves at the doorstep
could land sea-borne coal.

36
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:22,679
And the Federated Malay
States Railway station

37
00:02:22,759 --> 00:02:26,550
nearby could bring in coal
and materials by rail.

38
00:02:26,550 --> 00:02:30,918
In 1924 the Municipality bought the

39
00:02:30,998 --> 00:02:35,700
65,000 square foot site for $375,000.

40
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:39,867
The swamp was reclaimed and
levelled, foundation work began

41
00:02:39,947 --> 00:02:45,193
late that year, and by Christmas 1925
the foundations of the boiler house,

42
00:02:45,273 --> 00:02:48,800
turbine house and switchgear
house were complete.

43
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:52,848
The station was designed by
the Chief Municipal Architect,

44
00:02:52,928 --> 00:02:56,194
Alexander Gordon — the
architect of City Hall —

45
00:02:56,274 --> 00:02:59,050
with Preece, Cardew and Rider advising.

46
00:02:59,050 --> 00:03:03,097
Behind an Edwardian red-brick
facade with full-length

47
00:03:03,177 --> 00:03:07,847
tinted-glass windows stood a
steel skeleton of some 820 tons,

48
00:03:07,927 --> 00:03:10,962
six British boilers, and three turbines:

49
00:03:11,042 --> 00:03:15,325
one of 2,000 kilowatts and
two of 5,000 kilowatts each.

50
00:03:15,325 --> 00:03:18,800
Demand would not wait for the full plant.

51
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:22,395
The first unit, the
2,000 kilowatt generator,

52
00:03:22,475 --> 00:03:27,377
was installed and commissioned
on the 30th of September 1926,

53
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:32,275
running only from 6 to 11 in
the evening to shave the peak.

54
00:03:32,275 --> 00:03:36,022
As it ramped up, Mackenzie
Road's supply was

55
00:03:36,102 --> 00:03:40,450
wound down and ceased on
the 29th of October 1926.

56
00:03:40,450 --> 00:03:44,075
By the 1st of June 1927 Saint James was

57
00:03:44,155 --> 00:03:47,575
supplying the whole existing system.

58
00:03:47,575 --> 00:03:51,085
The Commissioners,
foreseeing still more demand,

59
00:03:51,165 --> 00:03:55,198
authorised an additional
10,000 kilowatt set that June,

60
00:03:55,278 --> 00:04:00,358
bringing the plant to about 22,000
kilowatts — almost seven times the

61
00:04:00,438 --> 00:04:04,850
roughly 3,200 kilowatts of
everything that had come before.

62
00:04:04,850 --> 00:04:10,375
The building itself was designed
to be extended to 40,000 kilowatts.

63
00:04:10,375 --> 00:04:14,090
On the 7th of November 1927
the station was officially

64
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:18,658
opened by Sir Hugh Clifford,
Governor of the Straits Settlements,

65
00:04:18,738 --> 00:04:21,469
who marked the novelty of the age with a

66
00:04:21,549 --> 00:04:25,475
story about a servant in
Nigeria asking to bring his wife

67
00:04:25,555 --> 00:04:29,350
to see a kettle boil water
from "a peg into the wall".

68
00:04:29,350 --> 00:04:32,694
The power reached some 28,255 people,

69
00:04:32,774 --> 00:04:38,050
besides street lighting,
tramways, the port and industry.

70
00:04:38,050 --> 00:04:43,555
Tariffs fell from 14 cents a unit
in 1927 to 6.2 cents in 1932,

71
00:04:43,635 --> 00:04:47,544
and in 1928 the Electricity
Department opened

72
00:04:47,624 --> 00:04:52,331
an office on Orchard Road
to teach the public to use —

73
00:04:52,411 --> 00:04:57,375
and to lease — electric
cookers, fans and water heaters.

74
00:04:57,375 --> 00:05:01,471
Saint James burned coal delivered
by sea to its own doorstep,

75
00:05:01,551 --> 00:05:06,000
and the supply line reached further
than most people would guess.

76
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:09,578
Singapore's coal initially
arrived from Manchuria,

77
00:05:09,658 --> 00:05:14,113
shipped through Japanese firms
that were the lowest tenderers,

78
00:05:14,193 --> 00:05:17,332
until that supply stopped
in the late 1930s;

79
00:05:17,412 --> 00:05:20,850
after that, coal came
from Peninsular Malaysia.

80
00:05:20,850 --> 00:05:25,438
But coal costs were rising, and
in 1940 the station switched

81
00:05:25,518 --> 00:05:30,575
from coal to fuel oil, with two
boilers converted for oil-firing.

82
00:05:30,575 --> 00:05:33,846
So the famous coal-fired
station burned coal

83
00:05:33,926 --> 00:05:37,200
for only about fourteen
of its fifty years.

84
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:40,820
The label is not wrong — coal
is what it was built for,

85
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:44,251
and coal shaped its site,
its wharves and its early

86
00:05:44,331 --> 00:05:47,547
working life — but the
greater part of its career

87
00:05:47,627 --> 00:05:51,125
ran on oil, and its last
machines were gas turbines.

88
00:05:51,125 --> 00:05:53,875
The early years were troubled.

89
00:05:53,875 --> 00:05:56,525
There were blackouts as early as 1928,

90
00:05:56,605 --> 00:06:00,765
and one shutdown that November
was traced to the negligence

91
00:06:00,845 --> 00:06:04,150
of junior shift engineers,
who were dismissed.

92
00:06:04,150 --> 00:06:07,749
Working the station was
hard, round-the-clock labour,

93
00:06:07,829 --> 00:06:13,175
and staff were expected to answer a
fault "in a matter of ten minutes or so".

94
00:06:13,175 --> 00:06:15,250
Then came the war.

95
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:18,806
When the expatriate engineers
were interned in Changi,

96
00:06:18,886 --> 00:06:23,182
local staff kept the station and
the distribution network running

97
00:06:23,262 --> 00:06:28,299
under the Japanese — two Japanese
supervisors over the distribution section,

98
00:06:28,379 --> 00:06:31,665
and Singaporean foremen
and assistants below them,

99
00:06:31,745 --> 00:06:34,775
improvising spare parts
off the black market.

100
00:06:34,775 --> 00:06:38,844
One wireman, Lim Loo Cheong,
recalled being fetched from

101
00:06:38,924 --> 00:06:42,925
home for cable faults and
paid in rice and vegetables.

102
00:06:42,925 --> 00:06:45,854
The war wrecked the plant all the same:

103
00:06:45,934 --> 00:06:50,019
by 1945 the turbines were
"all very seriously damaged"

104
00:06:50,099 --> 00:06:53,725
and the boiler house "in
deplorable condition".

105
00:06:53,725 --> 00:06:57,951
Demand jumped by about half after
the war, while the machinery

106
00:06:58,031 --> 00:07:02,475
was still on temporary repairs,
and the failures made headlines.

107
00:07:02,475 --> 00:07:06,461
On the 7th of February 1948
a generator breakdown cut

108
00:07:06,541 --> 00:07:11,064
power for eight and a half hours
across all non-city areas —

109
00:07:11,144 --> 00:07:14,750
the Straits Times mourned
the melted ice-cream.

110
00:07:14,750 --> 00:07:18,692
On the 19th of September 1950
a single generator failure

111
00:07:18,772 --> 00:07:22,570
cascaded into an island-wide
blackout of about an hour

112
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:27,885
and a half: babies were delivered by
lamplight at Kandang Kerbau Hospital,

113
00:07:27,965 --> 00:07:30,398
and a play at the Victoria Memorial

114
00:07:30,478 --> 00:07:34,500
Hall was lit by a car's
headlamps reflected in a mirror.

115
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:38,153
In January 1951 a welding accident at the

116
00:07:38,233 --> 00:07:41,875
station killed two men and injured four.

117
00:07:41,875 --> 00:07:45,153
The engineers, meanwhile,
fought the Monday-morning

118
00:07:45,233 --> 00:07:47,524
demand spike — the Monday Syndrome —

119
00:07:47,604 --> 00:07:51,225
by starting their sets at
three or four in the morning.

120
00:07:51,225 --> 00:07:55,745
By the mid-1950s the
verdict was inefficiency:

121
00:07:55,825 --> 00:08:00,745
in 1955 Saint James generated
at 3.57 cents a unit

122
00:08:00,825 --> 00:08:06,025
against the newer Pasir
Panjang station's 1.4 cents.

123
00:08:06,025 --> 00:08:11,257
The station closed for upgrading
in 1956, and the renovated plant

124
00:08:11,337 --> 00:08:17,467
was reopened on the 2nd of July 1960
by the Finance Minister, Goh Keng Swee,

125
00:08:17,547 --> 00:08:22,450
with new machines that increased
output by 18,000 kilowatts.

126
00:08:22,450 --> 00:08:26,141
The two tall chimneys that
define the building today

127
00:08:26,221 --> 00:08:30,274
date from this rebuild; the
west chimney, 32 metres high,

128
00:08:30,354 --> 00:08:33,400
now houses the station's heritage gallery.

129
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:37,315
In 1963 the Public Utilities
Board was formed to

130
00:08:37,395 --> 00:08:41,143
manage Singapore's
electricity, water and gas,

131
00:08:41,223 --> 00:08:46,050
and Saint James ran under the
PUB for its remaining years.

132
00:08:46,050 --> 00:08:50,450
It was not enough to keep the
old station in the front rank.

133
00:08:50,450 --> 00:08:55,298
With the full opening of Pasir
Panjang Power Station in 1966,

134
00:08:55,378 --> 00:09:01,275
and Jurong Power Station following,
Saint James was gradually phased out.

135
00:09:01,275 --> 00:09:05,761
The last of its gas turbines
was decommissioned in 1976 —

136
00:09:05,841 --> 00:09:09,205
fifty years after the
first small generator

137
00:09:09,285 --> 00:09:13,050
had been switched on to
cover the evening peak.

138
00:09:13,050 --> 00:09:15,900
The building was not demolished.

139
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:20,638
In the early 1980s the Port of
Singapore Authority converted

140
00:09:20,718 --> 00:09:24,332
it into a high-bay,
semi-automated warehouse —

141
00:09:24,412 --> 00:09:30,275
described as Southeast Asia's first
fully automated commercial warehouse —

142
00:09:30,355 --> 00:09:34,450
which opened in 1983 and
served the PSA until 1992.

143
00:09:34,450 --> 00:09:37,241
After that the station sat largely vacant,

144
00:09:37,321 --> 00:09:41,150
while the HarbourFront precinct
was replanned around it.

145
00:09:41,150 --> 00:09:45,201
The second life began with
nightlife entrepreneur Dennis Foo,

146
00:09:45,281 --> 00:09:48,723
investing through Dennon
Entertainment with partners

147
00:09:48,803 --> 00:09:52,325
that included the state-owned
Mapletree Investments.

148
00:09:52,325 --> 00:09:56,221
The conversion cost about 40
million Singapore dollars —

149
00:09:56,301 --> 00:09:59,628
half from Mapletree,
primarily for conservation,

150
00:09:59,708 --> 00:10:03,400
and half from the other
investors for the interiors.

151
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:08,449
Keeping the name Saint James Power
Station, the complex officially

152
00:10:08,529 --> 00:10:14,510
launched on the 24th of September 2006
with 12 outlets for live entertainment,

153
00:10:14,590 --> 00:10:18,475
music and dining, holding
more than 10,000 people.

154
00:10:18,475 --> 00:10:22,646
In its later years it was
described as 11 nightclubs and

155
00:10:22,726 --> 00:10:27,655
live-entertainment venues under
one roof — Dragonfly for Mandopop,

156
00:10:27,735 --> 00:10:31,075
The Boiler Room for
rock and R&B among them.

157
00:10:31,075 --> 00:10:33,206
Midway through the party years,

158
00:10:33,286 --> 00:10:36,425
the building received
its formal protection.

159
00:10:36,425 --> 00:10:41,228
On the 11th of November 2009 the
National Heritage Board gazetted

160
00:10:41,308 --> 00:10:46,336
Saint James Power Station a national
monument — the 60th building or

161
00:10:46,416 --> 00:10:51,600
site so gazetted — while the nightclubs
were still trading inside it.

162
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:54,365
In 2010 the conversion won the

163
00:10:54,445 --> 00:10:57,575
URA Architectural Heritage Award.

164
00:10:57,575 --> 00:11:00,945
The clubs ran on until the lease expired,

165
00:11:01,025 --> 00:11:04,475
and the complex closed in September 2018.

166
00:11:04,475 --> 00:11:08,306
In November 2019 Mapletree
announced that the monument

167
00:11:08,386 --> 00:11:11,420
would be restored with
Dyson as its tenant,

168
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:15,700
as part of the Greater Southern
Waterfront transformation.

169
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:18,968
The restoration inserted
floating floor slabs and

170
00:11:19,048 --> 00:11:23,615
atriums into the cavernous halls,
conserved the facade and chimneys,

171
00:11:23,695 --> 00:11:26,280
fitted a heritage gallery into the west

172
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:30,050
chimney and laid a heritage
trail around the building.

173
00:11:30,050 --> 00:11:34,335
On the 25th of March 2022
Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong

174
00:11:34,415 --> 00:11:39,401
officially opened Dyson's new
global headquarters at Saint James,

175
00:11:39,481 --> 00:11:43,300
with the company's founder,
James Dyson, present.

176
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:47,117
The restored monument
holds 110,000 square feet;

177
00:11:47,197 --> 00:11:54,019
more than 1,400 Dyson people work in Singapore,
560 of them engineers and scientists,

178
00:11:54,099 --> 00:11:57,836
and the company announced
a further 1.5 billion

179
00:11:57,916 --> 00:12:02,625
Singapore dollars of Singapore
investment over four years.

180
00:12:02,625 --> 00:12:07,493
The heritage gallery opened the
following month, and the restoration

181
00:12:07,573 --> 00:12:11,931
won the URA Architectural Heritage
Award for Conservation and

182
00:12:12,011 --> 00:12:17,250
Innovation (Distinction) in 2022 —
the building's second heritage award.

183
00:12:17,250 --> 00:12:20,865
A century after its first
generator was commissioned,

184
00:12:20,945 --> 00:12:25,187
the coal station is a technology
company's world headquarters,

185
00:12:25,267 --> 00:12:28,125
and its chimney carries the word "dyson".

186
00:12:28,125 --> 00:12:30,370
The harbour at its doorstep has

187
00:12:30,450 --> 00:12:33,300
changed as completely as the building.

188
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:37,215
The coal wharves are gone;
the gas that now does the work

189
00:12:37,295 --> 00:12:40,720
coal once did arrives by
pipeline and by ship at a

190
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:44,715
terminal on Jurong Island —
a story this blog has told in

191
00:12:44,795 --> 00:12:48,650
The Pipelines That Feed
Singapore and The LNG Terminal.

192
00:12:48,650 --> 00:12:51,599
Saint James stands at
the start of that arc:

193
00:12:51,679 --> 00:12:55,936
the place where Singapore first
built power at municipal scale,

194
00:12:56,016 --> 00:12:58,150
in brick, on a reclaimed swamp.

195
00:12:58,150 --> 00:13:02,195
A century on, Singapore's
best-known power station is famous

196
00:13:02,275 --> 00:13:05,907
for everything except power
— the nightclub it became,

197
00:13:05,988 --> 00:13:09,895
the headquarters it now houses
— but each of its lives has

198
00:13:09,975 --> 00:13:14,100
run inside the same Edwardian
shell that first lit the town.
